  "description": "EWUXAX crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group C 2/c. Reported CIF formula moiety: C78 H174 Co2 Gd6 N6 O45 P6,10(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Gd1 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd2 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd3 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Co1 (Co) has 4 O neighbors; Gd1A (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd2A (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd3A (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Co1A (Co) has 4 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 11 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.257-4.303 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 95.88-129.75°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [CoIII2GdIII6(μ3-OH)2(μ2-OH)(tBuPO3)4(tBuPO3H)2(O2CtBu)3(HO2CtBu)3(deaH)2(deaH2)4]·10H2O. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 2 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 1 μ2-OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula). Article name explicitly identifies Co(III), Gd(III).",
